          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On August 11, 2013, around midnight, a witness observed in the clear sky several orange-colored objects that stood out from the stars. Their movement from east to southeast was slow, and the witness took several photographs. The witness's description is entirely consistent with the observation of Thai lanterns, which are fairly common summer nights in cities: round, orange lights flying continuously. The objects moved towards southeast: the weather report for Quimper indicates a light west wind, generally consistent with the objects' movement carried by the wind. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\": probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
